---
// src/pages/press.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Press Release: WristTrack 2.0 | WristTrack">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <!-- Top Back Link & Metadata -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-sm font-medium text-[#39a5c0] hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1 mb-6"
      >
        ← Back to WristTrack
      </a>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
        <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#39a5c0]/10 text-[#39a5c0]">For Immediate Release</span>
        <span>Glasgow, UK — November 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Body using @tailwindcss/typography -->
    <article class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert lg:prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-bold prose-a:text-[#39a5c0] prose-blockquote:border-l-[#39a5c0]">
      <h1>
        WristTrack Celebrates Three Years with Landmark 2.0 Release, Bringing Optional Cloud Sync, Multi-Device Support, and Unrivalled Collection Analytics
      </h1>

      <p class="lead">
        <strong>GLASGOW, UK — November 2026</strong> — WristTrack, the dedicated collection and wear-tracking app built for watch enthusiasts, today announces the launch of <strong>WristTrack 2.0</strong>. Arriving as the app celebrates its third anniversary, this milestone update represents the biggest evolution in WristTrack’s history—introducing seamless multi-device cloud sync while staying fiercely committed to a local-first, offline-safe architecture.
      </p>

      <p>
        Over the past three years, WristTrack has grown organically from a simple tool for visualising basic wrist-time charts into a comprehensive horological database. Today, collectors use the app to log and collate a wealth of data—from wear stats, water resistance, and lug measurements to daily timing accuracy against atomic time servers.
      </p>

      <p>
        With version 2.0, collectors can now take that data across all their devices without sacrificing privacy or offline reliability.
      </p>

      <h2>Key Highlights of WristTrack 2.0</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local-First Cloud Sync:</strong> Users can now optionally sync their entire watch collection and wear history across multiple devices. True to WristTrack’s core philosophy, the app remains 100% local-first and offline-safe—meaning your data always lives on your device first, works anywhere without an internet connection, and syncs seamlessly when you’re back online.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Expanded Device Support:</strong> WristTrack 2.0 introduces official, layout-optimised support for <strong>iPad</strong>, <strong>Android tablets</strong>, and <strong>foldable devices</strong> (including the iPhone Duo), giving collectors a larger canvas to explore their analytics and high-resolution watch photography.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Biometric App Lock:</strong> Collectors can now secure their personal collection logs and valuations behind Face ID, Touch ID, or fingerprint authentication.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Saved GMT Timezones (Pro):</strong> Frequent flyers and GMT watch owners on WristTrack Pro can now save multiple custom timezones for quick reference and effortless GMT hand setting.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Unmatched Data Filtering in a Growing Space</h2>
      <p>
        While a handful of newer apps have recently entered the market allowing users to log what watch they wore on a given day, WristTrack 2.0 widens the gap in what collectors can actually <em>do</em> with that information.
      </p>
      <p>
        No other app offers the analytical depth of WristTrack’s charting engine. Collectors can slice, group, and filter their wear history by almost any recorded data point - whether by brand, colour, case diameter, or even by decade - across any custom timeframe. Instead of a static logbook, WristTrack turns years of wrist time into actionable insights about how a collection is truly worn and enjoyed.
      </p>

      <h2>A Note to the Community</h2>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          Three years ago, WristTrack started as a passion project to solve a simple problem: I wanted a better way to see which watches in my watch box were actually getting wrist time. Seeing it evolve into the rich analytics platform it is today - and watching collectors rely on it daily - has been incredible. None of this would exist without the encouragement, bug reports, and brilliant feature ideas from the watch enthusiast community. Thank you for helping shape WristTrack into what it is today.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>WristTrack 2.0</strong> is available now as a free update for existing users on the <strong>Apple App Store</strong> and <strong>Google Play Store</strong>, with optional Pro features available via in-app upgrade.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Media Kit / Contact Footer Box -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Media & Press Enquiries</p>
        <p>
          Email: <a href="mailto:grant@wristtrack.app?subject=WristTrack%202.0%20Press%20Enquiry" class="text-[#39a5c0] hover:underline">grant@wristtrack.app</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          Instagram: <a href="https://instagram.com/wristtrack.app" class="text-[#39a5c0] hover:underline">@wristtrack.app</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-[#39a5c0] text-white font-medium hover:bg-[#1B6B82] transition-colors self-start sm:self-center"
      >
        Download WristTrack 2.0
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
